        en: 'Last lesson answered one question: is the pattern there? Real data questions ask: what is the value itself? Give me the address, give me the number. Today we learn findall — the method that refuses to stop at yes or no and harvests everything matching the pattern from inside the line. By the end of this lesson you will be able to: use re.findall to pull lists of matches, read the pattern \\S+@\\S+ character by character, tell search().group() apart from findall, and build a len(x) > 0 filter over whole lines.',
