          en: 'The book\u2019s application: a loop over mailbox lines, inside it x = re.findall(r"\\S+@\\S+", line), then if len(x) > 0: print(x). Since findall returns a list, its length is the test — the chapter-8 guardian habit in a new language. But inspect the harvest critically: headers like Return-Path: yield addresses with junk attached such as <, ; and ) — because \\S accepts any non-space character, anything but a blank. We tighten the pattern next lesson with character classes.',
